{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/161935-inspiring-fantasy-and-dark-fantasy-films-and-tv-shows","id":161935,"title":"Inspiring fantasy and dark fantasy films and TV shows","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-07T12:47:38-07:00","id":161935,"title":"Inspiring fantasy and dark fantasy films and TV shows","content":"I'm running a mage the Ascension game set in the mythic ages and I want some inspiration for my game hat doesn't come from video games and books, any recommendations?<br /> <br /> The game has heavy fantasy elements, including some which were taken from Dark Ages Fae and even Werewolf and of course, Mage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:23:46-07:00","id":163035,"title":"","content":"Merin was a fun show though not dark at all. Made even better if you play the drinking game while watching.<br /> <br /> Of course if you want mythic age, nothing better than fantasy movies from the 80's. Dragon Slayer, Conan the Barbarian, Willow. High Fantasy and anything possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T21:49:24-07:00","id":164474,"title":"","content":"Honesetly, Game of Thrones might work well for atmosphere. Just understand there's very little *actual* magic in it, except in a few cases, and it's made clear most of the normals dont' believe in magic. Supposedly, all magic faded away when the kingdom of Old Valeryia was destroying in some undefined cataclysm. The handful of rare artifacts (like Valyrian Steel swords) purportedly have a bit of magic left over, but it really is the Dark Ages for that world. But if you want the MOOD for a Dark Ages game of any venue, I can't recommend it enough.<br /> <br /> I just hope you don't get too attached to characters. The &quot;Main Character Shield&quot; (tm) does not exist.<br /> <br /> Unless you're Peter Dinklage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T15:09:19-07:00","id":165254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/161935-inspiring-fantasy-and-dark-fantasy-films-and-tv-shows?p=164474#post164474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honesetly, Game of Thrones might work well for atmosphere. Just understand there's very little *actual* magic in it, except in a few cases, and it's made clear most of the normals dont' believe in magic. Supposedly, all magic faded away when the kingdom of Old Valeryia was destroying in some undefined cataclysm. The handful of rare artifacts (like Valyrian Steel swords) purportedly have a bit of magic left over, but it really is the Dark Ages for that world. But if you want the MOOD for a Dark Ages game of any venue, I can't recommend it enough.<br /> <br /> I just hope you don't get too attached to characters. The &quot;Main Character Shield&quot; (tm) does not exist.<br /> <br /> Unless you're Peter Dinklage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've already read the first five books and won't watch the show, I find it interferes with my ability to imagine the characters and the contents of the novels when I watch TV shows and movies based on the books I read but thanks for your suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T19:11:53-07:00","id":165497,"title":"","content":"Have you checked out Ninja Scroll, Princess Mononoke, Tales from EarthSea and some of the other fantastic fantasy Anime that's out there? Spirited Away and Howl's moving Castle are more child oriented than the previous three but are still quite interesting and Nausica and the Valley of the Wind, while more science fiction than fantasy, is well worth checking out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T22:03:18-07:00","id":165628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream_Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/161935-inspiring-fantasy-and-dark-fantasy-films-and-tv-shows?p=165497#post165497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you checked out Ninja Scroll, Princess Mononoke, Tales from EarthSea and some of the other fantastic fantasy Anime that's out there? Spirited Away and Howl's moving Castle are more child oriented than the previous three but are still quite interesting and Nausica and the Valley of the Wind, while more science fiction than fantasy, is well worth checking out</div> </div> </div> </div>Prettymuch everything from Miyazaki is excellent inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T02:58:11-07:00","id":167705,"title":"","content":"Try Cadfael, the series about an abbot living in the Dark Ages. He's a retired old soldier who works as a healer and chemist and occasionally works as a detective. It's a bit on the lower scale of the fantasy spectrum, but the flavour and style are hard to beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T18:47:30-07:00","id":168480,"title":"","content":"<u><b>For Dark Ages: Werewolf:</b></u> The Company of Wolves (Movie)<br /> There's also Ladyhawke (Movie).<br /> <br /> Nash (<i>Of <a href=\"http://www.radiodeadair.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Radio Dead Air</a></i><a href=\"http://www.radiodeadair.com/\" target=\"_blank\">)</a>, has a review series that covers fantasy movies called <a href=\"http://thatguywiththeglasses.com/videolinks/teamt/nash/specials\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Here There Be Dragons&quot;</a>. So far, what he has covered has been: Willow, Krull, The Last Unicorn, Legend, and Dragonslayer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 06-13-2014, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:",